BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE H.902
2026 Page 1 of 2
1 H.902
2 Introduced by Representatives Boutin of Barre City and Waszazak of Barre
3 City
4 Referred to Committee on
5 Date:
6 Subject: Municipal and county government; municipal charters; City of Barre;
7 amendment
8 Statement of purpose of bill as introduced: This bill proposes to approve
9 amendments to the charter of the City of Barre to authorize the City Manager
10 or any councilor duly authorized by an action of the City Council to authorize
11 the sale of City property. This bill also proposes to amend City of Barre
12 charter provisions related to the City’s undesignated fund balance.
13 An act relating to approval of amendments to the charter of the City of
14 Barre
15 It is hereby enacted by the General Assembly of the State of Vermont:
16 Sec. 1. CHARTER AMENDMENT APPROVAL
17 The General Assembly approves the amendments to the charter of the City
18 of Barre as set forth in this act. The voters of the City approved the proposals
19 of amendment on May 13, 2025.

BILLAS PASSED BY THE HOUSE H.902
2026 Page 2 of 2
1 Sec. 2. 24 App. V.S.A. chapter 1 is amended to read:
2 CHAPTER 1. CITY OF BARRE
3 * * *
4 § 313. SALE OR LEASE OF CITY PROPERTY
5 The City Council may authorize the sale or lease of any real or personal
6 estate belonging to the City, and all conveyances, grants, or leases of such real
7 estate shall be signed by the Mayor, the City Manager, or any councilor duly
8 authorized by an action of the City Council.
9 * * *
10 § 601. PAYMENT OF TAXES
11 * * *
12 (b) At the close of the fiscal year audit, any unexpended funds remaining
13 from the City budget may be retained, if approved by vote of the City Council,
14 as an undesignated fund balance for future use. Any funds retained pursuant
15 to this provision shall be limited to an amount not greater than five 10 percent
16 of the City general fund budget expenses for the most recent voter-approved
17 fiscal year. Any amount remaining in excess of five percent in the City budget
18 such amount must be used in the subsequent budget to cut reduce the taxrate.
19 * * *
20 Sec. 3. EFFECTIVE DATE
21 This act shall take effect on passage.

